  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194756": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Laboratory Professor - Spring 2027 (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Chemistry Location: Middlebury, VT Visiting Assistant Laboratory Professor - Spring 2027 (Organic Chemistry ) The Department of Chemistry invites applications for a one-semester, full-time, position for Spring 2027. Applicants should have a Ph.D. / M.S. (preferred) or a B.A. / B.S. (with experience) in Chemistry or a closely related field. A demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching organic chemistry laboratory is expected. Responsibilities of the position include the preparation, teaching, and grading of three sections of Organic Chemistry I lab and one section of Organic Chemistry II lab in collaboration with a current organic lab professor teaching other sections of the established CHEM 0205/0305 lab curriculum. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, four-month, salaried position with a hiring range of $34,858 – $37,014 per semester. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/194756 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Prof. Rick Bunt, Search Chair; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching philosophy; and at least two confidential letters of recommendation that speak to teaching. Do not wait for all recommendation letters to arrive before submitting your application via Interfolio. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/194756 and at Additional information for CHEM Faculty Applicants .  Review of applications will begin on October 19 th and continue until the position is filled. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194753": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Laboratory Professor (General Chemistry)",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Chemistry Location: Middlebury, VT Visiting Assistant Laboratory Professor (General Chemistry) The Department of Chemistry invites applications for a two-year, full-time position starting in Spring 2027 and extending through Spring 2029. Applicants should have a Ph.D. (preferred) or M.S. in chemistry. Experience teaching chemistry laboratory is expected. Responsibilities of the position include the preparation, teaching and grading of four sections of General Chemistry laboratory per semester in collaboration with current lab professors teaching other sections of the established CHEM 0105 lab curriculum. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $69,717 - $74,029 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/194753 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Prof. Rick Bunt, Search Chair; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching philosophy; and at least two confidential letters of recommendation that speak to teaching. Do not wait for all recommendation letters to arrive before submitting your application via Interfolio. More information is available at [https://apply.interfolio.com/194753] and at Additional information for CHEM Faculty Applicants . Review of applications will begin on October 19 th and continue until the position is filled. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188301": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Modern Chinese Language, Literature, and Culture",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Chinese Location: Middlebury, VT Assistant Professor of Modern Chinese Language, Literature, and Culture, Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT — The Greenberg-Starr Department of Chinese invites applicants for a tenure-track position in modern Chinese language, literature, and culture beginning fall 2027. Candidates may be specialists in any genre of modern Chinese literature or other form of Chinese cultural production, including poetry, prose, and drama, as well as topical courses not confined to a single historical period, with priority given to candidates whose first area of expertise is the literature and culture of the People’s Republic of China, including that of the 21st century. Candidates with experience and demonstrated success teaching Chinese language, literature, and culture to undergraduate students are especially encouraged to apply. Applicants must have the Ph.D. in hand or expected by September 2027. Appointment is at the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidates must be committed to high quality undergraduate education, including language education and the mentoring of a diverse student population, and they also must be willing to dedicate themselves to participation in a department with a tradition of teamwork and team teaching. The successful candidate must have native or near-native proficiency in Modern Standard Chinese (“Mandarin”) and English and be eager to teach both Chinese language courses and courses in English on Chinese literature and culture. The typical teaching load will be 2 fall semester courses and 2 spring semester courses plus 1 Winter Term course in every other year, with Winter Term off in the alternate year. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462-$103,138 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/188301 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Department Chair Carrie Wiebe; a curriculum vitae; graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching and research plans; a sample of scholarly work; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/188301 and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/chinese . The application deadline is November 1, 2026, but review of completed applications will begin immediately, with priority given to applications received by October 1, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189955": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Architectural Studies",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of History of Art and Architecture Location: Middlebury College,  MIDDLEBURY, VT  The Department of History of Art & Architecture at Middlebury College invites applicants for a full-time tenure-track position in Architectural Studies beginning in fall 2027. The successful candidate for this position will have a strong commitment to, and training in, history and theory, as well as expertise in design methodology. They will be expected to teach foundational and upper-level architectural design studios, as well as theory courses. They will contribute to the department’s Museum Studies curriculum and team-taught global survey. A focus in Museum Studies or exhibition design is especially welcome. Applicants are required to have a MArch degree, with strong preference given to candidates holding a MArch and PhD, experience as the instructor of record teaching undergraduates, an active research agenda, and a commitment to the Liberal Arts. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/189955 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Carrie Anderson ; a curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy and research plans; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise . More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/189955 and our department website: https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/history-art-architectural-studies . The application deadline is December 1, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188680": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Italian",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Italian Location: Middlebury, VT Assistant Professor in Italian, Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT .  The Department of Italian invites applicants for a tenure-track position in Italian beginning Fall 2027.  The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in Italian language teaching and a Ph.D. They must be able to teach courses in both Italian and English; teaching responsibilities include language courses and literature/culture courses at all undergraduate levels in Italian. Research specialization is open, but preference will be given to candidates who can teach courses on topics such as contemporary Italian culture and politics, immigration, representation, identity, and colonialism that might contribute to interdisciplinary programs such as Black Studies and/or Comparative Literature. The successful candidate will be expected to teach two courses per semester, and one Winter Term every other year. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462-103,138 per year. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to Stefano Mula , Search Committee Chair. The letter should focus on the candidate’s pedagogical approach to teaching, their prior experience teaching Italian at the college level, content courses in English that the candidate would be interested to teach, and the candidate’s research portfolio and interests. In addition: 1) a curriculum vitae; 2) undergraduate and graduate transcripts; 3) a statement of teaching; 4) and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise; 5) a 20-25 page sample of scholarly writing. Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to Stefano Mula, Professor of Italian and Chair of the Italian Department, at smula@middlebury.edu . More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/188680 and our department website: https://www.middlebury.edu/academics/italian . The application deadline is October 15th, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188443": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Luso-Hispanic Studies",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Luso-Hispanic Studies Location: Middlebury, Vermont The Department of Luso-Hispanic Studies invites applicants for a full-time tenure-track position in Spanish beginning fall 2027. We seek candidates working in Latin American cultural studies who complement our current teaching and scholarship by specializing in one or more of these areas of study : democracy, the environment, and feminisms. Candidates must provide evidence of excellence in scholarship and teaching. Candidates must be strongly committed to teaching language courses at all levels and contributing to the college-wide curriculum, including in the First-Year Seminar program (in English) and Winter Term. Tenure-track faculty at Middlebury teach a 2/2 load with an additional class in winter term every other year. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College collect s all faculty job applications electronically at this link https://apply.interfolio.com/188443 . At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings. Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to the search committee chair , Professor Irina Feldman ; a curriculum vitae ; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promi se. Additi ona l material s such as transcripts and writing samples m ay be solic ited as the s earch progresses. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/188443 and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/luso-hispanic-studies . The application deadline is October 23 , 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecksLinks to an external site."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193054": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 09, 2026 Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Mathematics and Statistics Location: Middlebury, Vermont Assistant Professor of Mathematics and Statistics, Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT . The Department of Mathematics and Statistics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position in Mathematics and Statistics to begin in Fall 2027.  A Ph.D. in Mathematics or a closely related field should normally be in hand by time of appointment. The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Middlebury is a thriving program that supports majors in mathematics, applied mathematics, and statistics. The department seeks a candidate at the intersection of mathematics, applied mathematics, and statistics who can teach core courses and create cross-disciplinary electives that appeal to students across our program . The successful candidate will advise, mentor, and teach courses at all levels. In particular, we seek candidates who can contribute to our introductory sequences in both calculus and statistics. Candidates who demonstrate a capacity to include undergraduates in their research are especially encouraged to apply. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury's First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings, as described in our teaching load guidelines.  All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering an open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from myriad life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. Please submit: a letter of application; a teaching statement that includes your vision for teaching in a liberal arts setting; a description of your research program that includes ways you might include undergraduate students; curriculum vitae; graduate transcript; and three letters of recommendation, at least two of which speak to teaching ability.  Throughout your materials, please describe how your teaching and research would intersect with our departmental concentrations in mathematics, applied mathematics, and statistics . At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings. In your application materials, please also discuss how your teaching, research, and/or service would support our commitment to an open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. Questions about the application process or the position can be directed to Emily Proctor (eproctor@middlebury.edu). More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/193054 and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/mathematics . Applications received by October 21, 2026 will be guaranteed full consideration. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187640": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Philosophy Location: Middlebury, VT The Department of Philosophy seeks a full-time Assistant Professor for a tenure-track position, beginning September 2027, in AOS: Epistemology (especially Applied Epistemology, Social Epistemology, Political Epistemology, Feminist Epistemology, Virtue Epistemology), AOC: Open, but willing and able to teach one section of our introductory formal logic class annually. In addition to their scholarly program, the successful candidate will have broad philosophical interests and will be a dynamic and engaging teacher committed to working with students with diverse interests and backgrounds. The standard teaching load is 2-2, with an additional Winter Term course every other year. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462-$103,452 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link: https://apply.interfolio.com/187640 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Professor John Spackman; a curriculum vitae; graduate transcripts; statements of teaching and research plans (maximum 2 pages each); a writing sample of 25-30 pages; and at least three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/187640 and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/philosophy . The application deadline has been extended to October 30, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks/ ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188651": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Physics Location: Middlebury, VT Assistant Professor of Physics , Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT -- The Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in experimental physics, beginning Fall 2027.  We seek an intellectually vigorous individual who is committed to excellence in both teaching and research, and who will contribute to Middlebury ’s c ollege -wide liberal arts mission . Candidates should provide evidence of commitment to excellent teaching at all levels and potential to develop a strong research program involving undergraduate participation . Candidates are expected to hold a Ph . D . in experimental physics or a closely related field, with post-doctoral experience strongly preferred . The field of specialization within experimental physics is open, but candidates who will provide on-campus research opportunities for students are particularly encouraged to apply. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College collect s all faculty job applications electronically at https://apply.interfolio.com/188651 . Through Interfolio , submit an application addressed to Noah Graham, Department of Physics and Astronomy Chair , including curriculum vitae, unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, statement s of teaching and research plans, and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability /promise . Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and end when the position has been filled. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/188651 and at https://go.middlebury.edu/physics . Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188248": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Political Science Location: Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT The Department of Political Science invites applicants for a tenure-track position in Comparative Politics with a focus on African politics beginning fall 2027. We seek broadly trained candidates who will have completed a Ph.D. by the time of appointment and who are prepared to teach the introductory course in comparative politics as well as a variety of upper-level courses on African politics. Appointment will be made at the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidates should provide evidence of commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarly potential. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also periodically contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and, once tenured, serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically via this link https://apply.interfolio.com/188248 . Review of applications begins September 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Through the link, please submit: a letter of application addressed to the search committee chair, Professor Ajay Verghese; a curriculum vitae; a sample of scholarly production; evidence of teaching effectiveness; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching and research plans; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/188248 and Open Positions | Middlebury College ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189953": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Religion",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Religion Location: Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT The Religion Department at Middlebury College invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the rank of assistant professor in Applied Ethics beginning fall 2027. The field of specialization is open with respect to religious traditions, geographical regions, and major ethical topics. The successful candidate must be grounded in at least one religious tradition and able to teach courses on ethics at the intersections of religion and medicine and/or technology. Beyond this expectation, other possible areas may include religious perspectives on information, media, legal or environmental ethics. Our faculty have significant freedom to develop courses according to their own intellectual interests. Teaching responsibilities would include at least one course on medical ethics and/or bioethics as well as lectures and seminars on other topics in ethics. The successful candidate will also be prepared to contribute to our team-taught “Introduction to Religion” course and a senior seminar in theories and methods in the study of religion. There may also be opportunities to contribute to other interdisciplinary programs such as International and Global Studies; Gender, Sexuality, and Feminist Studies; Environmental Studies; Comparative Literature; Black Studies; and Privilege and Poverty. Our department is deeply committed to undergraduate teaching, and the ideal candidate will share that investment. We also collectively represent a wide range of methodological approaches to the study of religion, and we regularly engage in conversation about the differences in our training as well as our shared research and teaching interests. As part of a full-time teaching load, the candidate will contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. To apply, submit through Interfolio using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/189953 a cover letter, CV, graduate transcript, and the names of three recommenders, at least two of whom can speak to the candidate's teaching ability. Questions about this position should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Professor Jennifer Ortegren ( jortegren@middlebury.edu ). The deadline for applications is October 1, 2026. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in both faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open, and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience to our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188532": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Russian",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Russian Location: Middlebury College Assistant Professor of Russian, Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT -- The Russian Department invites applicants for a full-time tenure-track position in Russian beginning fall 2027. Research specialization is open.  Applicants should demonstrate an ability to teach Russian literature and culture, native or near-native fluency in Russian and English, and interest and experience in teaching language at the undergraduate level. The position entails teaching Russian at all levels and courses in English on Russian culture and literature. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Through Interfolio, candidates must submit a cover letter addressed to Prof. Timothy Portice, chair of the search committee. The letter should focus on the candidate’s pedagogical approach to teaching, their prior experience teaching Russian to non-native speakers at the college level, content courses in English that the candidate would be interested to teach, and the candidate’s research portfolio and interests. In addition, the application must include (i) an up to date CV, (ii) a syllabus for a Russian language course that the candidate previously taught at the first or second year level, (iii) at least one syllabus of a content course in English that the candidate either previously taught or would like to teach in the future, (iv) a 20-25 page sample of scholarly writing, and (v) three confidential letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability.  Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to Timothy Portice, Associate Professor of Russian and Chair of the Russian Department, at tportice@middlebury.edu . To apply, please follow this link: https://apply.interfolio.com/188532 The deadline for submitting application materials is October 15, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecksLinks to an external site."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188584": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Studio Art with a focus in Painting",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College Location: Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VERMONT The Department of Studio Art invites applicants for a full-time tenure-track position in Painting beginning fall 2027. Applicants must be able to teach traditional painting processes across a variety of media, have a notable exhibition record and an active studio practice amenable to student participation, and engage with contemporary dialogue within the field. The candidate must participate in a vigorous, cross-disciplinary studio program within a liberal arts environment and demonstrate the ability to engage students across the College’s curriculum broadening the student’s and institution’s dialogue with contemporary art and culture. The successful candidate will be expected to teach two courses in painting and/or drawing in the fall, spring, and every other winter, as well as guide senior thesis work in painting. In addition to teaching, the candidate will also collaborate with fellow Studio Art faculty to develop visiting lecture and workshop programming. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury’s First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings. All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute to service to the College, including, but not limited to, committee membership and serving as Director or Chair of a Program or Department when asked. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $91,462 - $103,138 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/188584 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to the Chair of the Studio Art Department; a curriculum vitae, a pdf with up to 20 images of your own work through Interfolio, a pdf with up to 20 images of student work through Interfolio, and names of three recommenders from whom letters of recommendation may be requested, at least two of whom must be able to speak to teaching ability and promise. More information on the position is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/ and http://www.middlebury.edu/academics/art . The application deadline is October 15, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check.  Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188815": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Biology, Middlebury College, Middlebury, VT.",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Biology Location: Middlebury, VT Visiting Assistant Professor of Biology , Middlebury College, Middlebury, VT.  The Biology Department invites applicants for a full-time (2-year) appointment at the rank of Visiting Assistant Professor of Biology, beginning in Fall 2027. Applicants must have a Ph.D. by the position start date and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. The successful candidate will be expected to teach two lecture sections of an introductory course in ecology and evolution during one semester, and two lecture sections of an introductory course in cell biology and genetics during the other semester. In the second year, the candidate will additionally teach a winter term elective course within their area of expertise that will serve the biology curriculum.  Depending on research needs, a shared lab space may be available to the successful candidate if they wish to have an active research program. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $92,577 – $96,355 per year. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings.  Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to the David Allen, chair of the search committee; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching interests and philosophy; a one-page statement that addresses how your teaching and mentorship demonstrate commitment to and/or evidence of access and inclusion in your classroom; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at [URL FROM INTERFOLIO] and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/biology . For full consideration, all application materials must be received by 9/1/2026. The review process will begin 9/2/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecksLinks to an external site. Applicants must have a Ph.D. by the position start date and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to David Allen, chair of the search committee; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching interests and philosophy; a one-page statement that addresses how your teaching and mentorship demonstrate commitment to and/or evidence of access and inclusion in your classroom; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/biology . For full consideration, all application materials must be received by 9/1/2026. The review process will begin 9/2/2026 and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188335": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Biology, Middlebury College, Middlebury, VT.",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Biology Location: Middlebury, VT The Biology Department invites applicants for a full-time temporary (3-year) leave-replacement appointment at the rank of Visiting Assistant Professor of Biology.  The position will last from Fall 2027 through Spring 2030. The successful candidate will be expected to teach the lecture section of an introductory course in ecology and evolution as well as design and teach courses that will serve the biology curriculum and fall within their area of expertise.  Specifically, the candidate will teach laboratory courses that center on the organismal level and include field-based exercises that focus on skills to study organisms and ecosystems in the field.  The candidate will also teach a non-laboratory elective course in the Winter Term.  Depending on research needs, a shared lab space may be available to the successful candidate if they wish to have an active research program. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $92,577 - $96,355 per year. Applicants must have a Ph.D. by the position start date and demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to Kirsten Coe, search committee chair; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching interests and philosophy; a one-page statement that addresses how your teaching and mentorship demonstrate commitment to and/or evidence of access and inclusion in your classroom; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which speak to teaching ability/promise. https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/biology . For full consideration, all application materials must be received by 9/1/2026. The review process will begin 9/2/2026 and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195923": {
      "title": "Half-Time Laboratory Professor of Biology, Middlebury College",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Biology Location: Middlebury College, Middlebury, VT The Biology Department invites applicants for a half-time (2-year) Assistant Laboratory Professor position, beginning in July 2027.  Applicants must have a Ph.D. by the position start date and demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching.  The successful candidate will teach two sections of an introductory, 100-level laboratory in cell biology and genetics. In collaboration with two additional lab professors, they will develop laboratory curricula, prepare laboratory classes, and mentor and train undergraduate teaching assistants. Scheduling flexibility is required as the lab sections may need to be offered in the evening. This is a 9-month contract, benefits-eligible position. The position does not offer resources for an individual research program. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a half-time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $34,858-$37,014 per year. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings.  Through Interfolio submit: a letter of application addressed to the Sam Byrne, Associate Professor of Biology and Global Health; a curriculum vitae; undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching interests and philosophy; a one-page statement that addresses how your teaching and mentorship demonstrate commitment to and/or evidence of access and inclusion in your classroom.  You will also need three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/biology For full consideration, all application materials must be received by 1/3/27. The review process will begin 1/4/27and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189339": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Premodern Art History",
      "description": "Department: Middlebury: College: Department of History of Art and Architecture Location: Middlebury College, Middlebury Vermont The Department of History of Art and Architecture, Middlebury College invites applications for a Visiting Assistant Professor of Premodern Art History to teach for two academic years beginning in the fall semester of 2027. The successful candidate will hold a Ph.D. or ABD in Art or Architectural History and have college-level teaching experience. They will participate in the instruction of our introductory course and offer lectures and seminars in their areas of expertise. Applicants with specialties in premodern architectural history, Asia, and/or the Global South are encouraged to apply. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a truly open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from a myriad of life experiences, opinions, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full time, benefits eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $92,577 - 96,355 per year. Middlebury College collects all faculty job applications electronically using this link https://apply.interfolio.com/189339 . Through Interfolio, submit: a letter of application addressed to Carrie Anderson; a curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy and research plans; and three current letters of recommendation, at least two of which must speak to teaching ability/promise. More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/189339 and our department website: https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/history-art-architectural-studies . The application deadline is October 1, 2026. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193058": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Department: Middlebury: College: Department of Mathematics and Statistics Location: Middlebury, Vermont Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics and Statistics, Middlebury College, MIDDLEBURY, VT. The Department of Mathematics and Statistics invites applications for a three-year visiting assistant professor position in Mathematics and Statistics to begin in Fall 2027. A Ph.D. in Mathematics or a closely related field should normally be in hand by time of appointment. The department seeks applicants who will contribute to teaching core courses such as analysis as well as offer electives that augment our curriculum in pure and applied mathematics. The successful candidate will teach courses at all levels of the curriculum, from our introductory calculus sequence to our senior offerings. As part of a full teaching load, the candidate will also regularly contribute to Middlebury's First Year Seminar Program and Winter Term course offerings, as described in our teaching load guidelines.  All faculty at Middlebury are also expected to contribute service to the College. Middlebury College is a top-tier liberal arts college with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in faculty teaching, research, and service. It is also an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering an open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. The College hires faculty from myriad life experiences, cultures, frames of reference, social identities, and learning perspectives to help cultivate and advance innovation in our curriculum and to provide a rich and varied educational experience for our talented and distinguished student body. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, salaried position with a hiring range of $92,577 - $96,355 per year. Middlebury College uses Interfolio to collect all faculty job applications electronically. Email and paper applications will not be accepted. Please submit: a letter of application; a teaching statement that includes your vision for teaching mathematics in a liberal arts setting; a description of your research program; curriculum vitae; graduate transcript; and three letters of recommendation, at least two of which speak to teaching ability.  At Middlebury, we strive to make our campus a respectful, engaged community that embraces difference and a full range of views and opinions, with all the complexity and individuality each person brings. In your application materials, please address how your teaching, research, and/or service might support our commitment to an open and supportive learning, teaching, and working environment. Questions about the application process or the position can be directed to Emily Proctor (eproctor@middlebury.edu). More information is available at https://apply.interfolio.com/193058 and https://www.middlebury.edu/college/academics/mathematics . Applications received by December 1, 2026 will be guaranteed full consideration. Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information on our background check policy can be found here: http://go.middlebury.edu/backgroundchecks ."
    }
